.superpowers/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
docs/history.bundle
docs/recovery/
task-2-report.md
.venv/
venv/
# Generated bundles. samples/ is the committed reference corpus and is not
# written to by the app; /api/save and the exporter write here instead.
output/

# Build artifact: regenerated by Install-ODF-Shortcut.bat. The committed copy
# embedded one machine SID, hostname and user profile path, and worked nowhere
# else.
ODF Generator.lnk

# The IOC documents a pack needs but this repository does not ship. They are
# fetched by `python -m generator.sources` into the pack directory, and they
# are the IOC's to publish, not ours to redistribute. Authored rules live
# under Rules/*/rules/ and Rules/*/Disciplines/*/rules/ and are NOT matched
# by any of these patterns -- check that first if a rule file goes missing.
Rules/*/codes/
Rules/*/Disciplines/*/*.pdf
Rules/*/Disciplines/*/*.md
Rules/*/*.pdf
Rules/*/*.xlsx
# Converted IOC documents that land at the pack root (the GEN document, the
# Foundation Principles, the Common Codes definition). The negation matters:
# PROVENANCE.md sits here too and is ours, not the IOC's.
Rules/*/*.md
!Rules/*/PROVENANCE.md
# The validator's own onboarding notes travel under Rules/ in its repository
# and document that application, not this one. See PROVENANCE.md.
Rules/*/_reference/

# Per-pack ingestion by-products and staging: the hash of each document last
# ingested, what was parsed out of it, the provenance record, and the download
# staging area. All rebuilt from the documents; none of them describe anything
# a fresh clone holds.
# Depth-agnostic on purpose. Drafts are written per DISCIPLINE, at
# Rules/<pack>/Disciplines/<CODE>/.drafts/, so a Rules/*/ pattern misses all 25
# of them: following the README left `git status` showing 25 untracked
# directories of generated, IOC-derived rules, one `git add -A` away from being
# committed.
Rules/**/.incoming/
Rules/**/.drafts/
Rules/**/.sources.json
Rules/**/.ingestion_state.json
Rules/**/.dd_obligations.json
